        "heading": "Make your content relevant to local buying situations",
        "blocks": [
          { "type": "p", "text": "Local relevance comes from understanding everyday situations, not inserting a city name into every caption. A café in Chandigarh might explain seating suitability for a short work meeting, parking considerations and quieter hours. A boutique serving nearby towns could show delivery options and measurement guidance for customers who cannot visit in person." },
          { "type": "p", "text": "Language should follow the audience. English may work for some customers, while Hindi or Punjabi explanations may make a demonstration easier to follow for others. Add readable captions to spoken videos and avoid assuming that every viewer has sound on. Keep the offer and next step clear whichever language you choose." },
          { "type": "ul", "items": ["Build posts around actual questions from calls, shop visits and messages.", "Discuss seasonal needs such as winter clothing, festive gifting or school admissions only when relevant to your products.", "Mention real service coverage and practical conditions rather than adding unrelated location tags."] },
          { "type": "p", "text": "Use the ideas in a [social media content strategy](/articles/how-to-build-social-media-content-strategy) to organise these topics. Local content should make a nearby customer feel understood, not simply remind them where they live." }
        ]
